# Date Issue Analysis for Ticket #4471

We analyzed the 412 reports merged into ticket #4471 to identify the root causes of the date issues reported by tenants.

## Findings

### 1. Month/Day Date Format Swap
**Description:** A systemic error where dates are interpreted using the wrong format (swapping Day and Month), leading to dates like April 7th being recorded as July 4th.

- **Reports Covered:** 418
- **GitHub Ticket:** [Issue #1](https://github.com/Infinity0106/capstone/issues/1)

### 2. One-Day Date Offset
**Description:** A smaller set of reports where the booking dates are shifted by exactly one day.

- **Reports Covered:** 5
- **GitHub Ticket:** [Issue #2](https://github.com/Infinity0106/capstone/issues/2)

### 3. Causality Violation
**Description:** A rare case where the notification invite arrived at the customer before the booking was actually created in the system.

- **Reports Covered:** 1 (R-41236)
- **GitHub Ticket:** [Issue #3](https://github.com/Infinity0106/capstone/issues/3)

